 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "A closed 9.8 mm wide body resists dust and flux. The shaft is insulated, and the part snaps into the board on two frame legs."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Rotation and taper",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "Rotation travel runs from terminal 1 to terminal 3. With 1B the output follows travel almost in proportion. 3B starts slowly, passes 50 % at mid travel and flattens near the end. 15A stays low over the first two thirds, near 17 % at mid travel, then climbs steeply. 15C is read across terminals 2 and 3, against travel numbered from terminal 3: near 17 % at mid travel, then a steep climb above about 65 %."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Single and dual elements",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "Single-element parts take 50 V AC or 20 V DC and 0.05 W. Ganged dual parts are for AC signals only, at 50 V AC and 0.03 W, with the two elements tracking within 3 dB over the range from −40 dB to 0 dB."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Collar and shaft options",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "RK09D carries a 5 mm collar on the bushing and turns 300°; RK09K turns 280° and has a collar only when ordered. A centre detent is optional. With the shaft at full CCW, the flat sits 50° or 60° from vertical, by shaft variety."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Suited to: audio gear (compact stereos, portable sets, speaker systems), mixers and electronic musical instruments, and setting controls in flat-panel TVs, game consoles, copiers and refrigerator thermostats."
  }
